(--- The ledger's basics leaves, batch A -----------------------------

 docs/ledger/basics.md maps LANGUAGE.md's Basics section, lines 38
 through 291 (Vox 0.4.15 pin, commit
 c013105, 5882 lines) into numbered claims about program SHAPE rather
 than values: which statement belongs to which clause, and whether a
 given piece of source text is even part of the program's meaning at
 all. The oracle for every leaf below is therefore an EXECUTION COUNT -
 the generator knows how many times a witness statement should run, so
 it emits a counter and asserts it, the same 'ASSERT <ID>: expected <x>
 got <y>' / exit 95 convention every other surface uses.

 Rows covered here: BAS-07, BAS-09, BAS-10 (comment placement), BAS-11
 (comment mid-statement), BAS-12, BAS-13 (comment spanning lines and
 nesting), BAS-14 (parens inside a string literal), BAS-16 (blank-line
 count between top-level statements), BAS-17 (blank line force-closes a
 single open loop), BAS-24 (a comment-only line is not a paragraph
 break), BAS-41 (the same blank line force-closes a loop and its
 enclosing function together), BAS-43 (the rule applies uniformly to
 On error too), BAS-46 (a blank line right after a comma stays
 cosmetic). Every claim was hand-verified against both vox 0.4.14
 (installed) and the 0.4.15 stack before being encoded; the retained
 probes are docs/ledger/probes/basics/BAS-07.vox, BAS-11.vox, BAS-12.vox,
 BAS-14.vox, BAS-16.vox, BAS-17.vox, BAS-24.vox, BAS-41.vox, BAS-43.vox
 and BAS-46.vox.

 BAS-50 (indentation width has no effect) is NOT a leaf here - see the
 batch report: 'layout put indent' (this file's own neighbour above,
 driven under --layout random) already draws 0-16 columns per line with
 no rule pinning any particular width, which is the row's exact claim,
 predating this batch. BAS-51 (nested-if Otherwise attachment) and the
 rest of the ledger's remaining todo rows are left for the next batch;
 BAS-57 is excluded on purpose - INDEX.md already carries it as an open
 discrepancy (D2, an Otherwise across a blank line), so a leaf asserting
 either reading would be asserting one side of an unresolved question.)

(Scratch view, program level and 'clear'ed per call (the same Defect 17
 shape every other surface's scratch buffer avoids): used only to
 measure a text's byte length, since a text has no size property of its
 own (PROCEDURE.md 6a) - declare a buffer from it and read the buffer's
 size instead.)

a buffer called 'the basics scratch view' is "".

(A short, varied piece of English filler for a comment's own TEXT.
 LANGUAGE.md constrains where a comment may sit and how it nests, never
 what it says, so a single fixed wording would be an undeclared rule
 (CLAUDE.md) the moment it showed up in every program. Five phrase
 shapes, crossed with a word drawn from the buffers surface's shared
 vocabulary (reused here purely as English words, the same way
 'gen flow witness name' reuses it for witness names) - full range, no
 ruling constrains either draw.)

To 'gen basics remark'.
    a number called 'how many words' is gen_buffer_words's length.
    a number called 'the word pick' is 'rng below' of 'how many words'.
    a number called 'the word index' is 'the word pick' add 1.
    a text called word is element 'the word index' of gen_buffer_words.
    a number called 'the shape' is 'rng below' of 5.
    If 'the shape' is 0 then,
        Return a text, "a note about {word}".
    If 'the shape' is 1 then,
        Return a text, "see {word} for details".
    If 'the shape' is 2 then,
        Return a text, "{word}, checked".
    If 'the shape' is 3 then,
        Return a text, "double-checked against {word}".
    Return a text, "nothing unusual here, just {word}".

(A comment spanning 'the line count' physical lines, LANGUAGE.md:77
 (BAS-12) - each line its own remark, so the whole comment does not read
 as one word repeated.)

To 'gen basics spanning comment' with a number called 'the line count'.
    a text called 'the first remark' is 'gen basics remark'.
    a text called body is "({'the first remark'}".
    a number called 'lines built' is 1.
    While 'lines built' is less than 'the line count',
        a text called 'the next remark' is 'gen basics remark',
        Set body to "{body}\n{'the next remark'}",
        Set 'lines built' to 'lines built' add 1.
    a text called 'the closed comment' is "{body})".
    Return a text, 'the closed comment'.

(A comment nested 'the depth' parenthesis-pairs deep, LANGUAGE.md:70
 (BAS-13) - hand-verified to six levels, so the depth drawn never
 exceeds that.)

To 'gen basics nested comment' with a number called 'the depth'.
    a text called 'the remark' is 'gen basics remark'.
    a text called opening is "".
    a number called 'parens placed' is 0.
    While 'parens placed' is less than 'the depth',
        Set opening to "{opening}(",
        Set 'parens placed' to 'parens placed' add 1.
    a text called closing is "".
    Set 'parens placed' to 0.
    While 'parens placed' is less than 'the depth',
        Set closing to "{closing})",
        Set 'parens placed' to 'parens placed' add 1.
    a text called whole is "{opening}{'the remark'}{closing}".
    Return a text, whole.

(BAS-07, BAS-09, BAS-10 (LANGUAGE.md:56, 74, 75): a comment changes
 nothing, tried in the two positions that do not touch an existing
 statement's own tokens - standing alone on its own line between two
 statements, or sitting at the end of one, after its period. Which
 position appears is drawn at random, and so is the comment's own
 wording, so neither the position nor the words repeat identically
 across a corpus. Also covers BAS-08's worked example (the same shape,
 reproduced by hand at docs/ledger/probes/basics/BAS-07.vox).)

To 'gen leaf comment placement' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the tally name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the remark' is 'gen basics remark'.
    a text called 'the tally declaration' is "{indent}a number called {'the tally name'} is 0.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the tally declaration'.
    a number called 'the position' is 'rng below' of 2.
    If 'the position' is 0 then,
        a text called 'the standalone comment' is "{indent}({'the remark'})\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the standalone comment'.
    a text called 'the first action' is "{indent}Set {'the tally name'} to {'the tally name'} add 1.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the first action'.
    If 'the position' is 0 then,
        a text called 'the second action' is "{indent}Set {'the tally name'} to {'the tally name'} add 1.\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the second action'.
    If 'the position' is 1 then,
        a text called 'the trailing action' is "{indent}Set {'the tally name'} to {'the tally name'} add 1. ({'the remark'})\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the trailing action'.
    a text called 'the assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-07" and 'the tally name' and 2.
    a text called 'the assertion line' is "{indent}{'the assertion'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the assertion line'.

(BAS-11 (LANGUAGE.md:76): a comment can sit in the MIDDLE of a
 statement, between two tokens - inside a declaration, an expression, or
 an If condition. One position is drawn per emission; docs/ledger/
 probes/basics/BAS-11.vox hand-verifies all three in one program.)

To 'gen leaf comment mid statement' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the remark' is 'gen basics remark'.
    a number called 'the position' is 'rng below' of 3.
    If 'the position' is 0 then,
        'gen leaf comment mid declaration' of indent and 'the remark'.
    If 'the position' is 1 then,
        'gen leaf comment mid expression' of indent and 'the remark'.
    If 'the position' is 2 then,
        'gen leaf comment mid condition' of indent and 'the remark'.

(The value a mid-declaration comment sits beside is pure filler with
 respect to BAS-11's claim - any number would put the comment on trial
 equally well - so its MAGNITUDE is free, drawn from 'gen extreme
 number' (gen_core.vox:88) rather than a tame 'rng below' of 1000
 (Josj, 2026-08-20: "instead of always setting values to things like
 32.8 I wanna see 1243626351836374761..."). Asserted with 'gen assert
 number matches' rather than 'gen assert number is', since the value is
 TEXT (up to 18-19 digits, beyond what needs converting to a Vox
 `number` in the generator itself) - it is embedded directly as the
 expected EXPRESSION rather than round-tripped through a meta-generator
 number, so the check holds at any magnitude the helper can draw. Hand-
 verified against vox 0.4.14 and the 0.4.15 stack that a comment sitting
 between the type noun and `called` survives i64::MAX unchanged.)

To 'gen leaf comment mid declaration' with a text called indent and a text called remark.
    a text called 'the value name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the value' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a text called 'the value declaration' is "{indent}a number ({remark}) called {'the value name'} is {'the value'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the value declaration'.
    (Calls 'gen assert number' directly, NOT the 'matches' wrapper: that
     wrapper wraps its expected-expression argument in a `{…}` format
     slot for the failure message, correct when the argument is a
     variable reference whose live value should be shown, wrong here -
     'the value' is a bare LITERAL, and wrapping "9223372036854775807"
     in braces turns the printed message into an OUTPUT-PROGRAM format
     slot referencing a variable of that name, which does not exist
     ("Unknown variable: 9223372036854775807" - caught compiling 60
     samples off seeds 1-60, all failing this way, before this line
     existed). A bare literal is its own "shown" text - the same
     pattern 'gen assert number is' uses for an ordinary small number.)
    a text called 'the assertion' is 'gen assert number' of "BAS-11" and 'the value name' and 'the value' and 'the value'.
    a text called 'the assertion line' is "{indent}{'the assertion'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the assertion line'.

(Both operands are drawn from 'gen extreme number' too - LANGUAGE.md's
 own claim is about the comment's position, not the arithmetic, so the
 oracle here is AGREEMENT rather than a pre-computed sum: the same
 `left add right` is declared once with the comment spliced in and once
 without, and the two declared numbers must read identically. This
 sidesteps the generator needing to do i64 addition on up-to-18-digit
 operands itself (a wrong hand-computed expectation would be exactly
 the false-finding-factory risk CLAUDE.md warns about) and still
 exercises the boundary: hand-verified against vox 0.4.14 and the
 0.4.15 stack that `9223372036854775807 add 9223372036854775807`
 silently wraps to -2 on both compilers, identically whether the
 comment is there or not - overflow is real and reachable here, and the
 leaf is deliberately built so a genuine divergence between the two
 declarations (comment vs. no comment) would still be caught rather
 than one leaf's own wrong arithmetic masquerading as one.)

To 'gen leaf comment mid expression' with a text called indent and a text called remark.
    a text called 'the with comment name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the without comment name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the left' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a text called 'the right' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a text called 'the with comment declaration' is "{indent}a number called {'the with comment name'} is {'the left'} ({remark}) add {'the right'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the with comment declaration'.
    a text called 'the without comment declaration' is "{indent}a number called {'the without comment name'} is {'the left'} add {'the right'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the without comment declaration'.
    a text called 'the assertion' is 'gen assert number matches' of "BAS-11" and 'the with comment name' and 'the without comment name'.
    a text called 'the assertion line' is "{indent}{'the assertion'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the assertion line'.

(The tested value in an If condition, same reasoning as the declaration
 leaf above: 'gen extreme number' never draws negative (no minus sign
 anywhere in it or in 'gen random digits'), so "is greater than or
 equal to 0" still fires deterministically at every magnitude the
 helper can draw, and the comment's position is what is actually on
 trial. Hand-verified against vox 0.4.14 and the 0.4.15 stack with
 i64::MAX in this exact position.)

To 'gen leaf comment mid condition' with a text called indent and a text called remark.
    a text called 'the outcome name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the probe value' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a text called 'the outcome declaration' is "{indent}a number called {'the outcome name'} is 0.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the outcome declaration'.
    a text called 'the if line' is "{indent}If {'the probe value'} ({remark}) is greater than or equal to 0 then, Set {'the outcome name'} to 1.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the if line'.
    a text called 'the assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-11" and 'the outcome name' and 1.
    a text called 'the assertion line' is "{indent}{'the assertion'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the assertion line'.

(BAS-12, BAS-13 (LANGUAGE.md:66-70): a comment can span several physical
 lines, and parentheses can nest inside one, to at least six levels -
 both varied per emission, both proven cosmetic by the same tally the
 rest of this file's comment leaves use.)

To 'gen leaf comment multiline nested' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the tally name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the tally declaration' is "{indent}a number called {'the tally name'} is 0.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the tally declaration'.
    a number called 'the line count' is 'rng below' of 3 add 2.
    a text called 'the spanning comment' is 'gen basics spanning comment' of 'the line count'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the spanning comment'}\n".
    a text called 'the first action' is "{indent}Set {'the tally name'} to {'the tally name'} add 1.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the first action'.
    a number called 'the depth' is 'rng below' of 5 add 2.
    a text called 'the nested comment' is 'gen basics nested comment' of 'the depth'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the nested comment'}\n".
    a text called 'the second action' is "{indent}Set {'the tally name'} to {'the tally name'} add 1.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the second action'.
    a text called 'the assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-12" and 'the tally name' and 2.
    a text called 'the assertion line' is "{indent}{'the assertion'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the assertion line'.

(BAS-14 (undocumented precision, LANGUAGE.md's Comments section says
 nothing about string literals either way): parentheses inside a STRING
 LITERAL are ordinary text, not a comment. The generator built the
 literal, so it knows its exact byte length; declaring a buffer from the
 printed copy and reading the buffer's size is how that gets checked -
 if the parens had instead been read as a comment opener, the compiler
 would refuse the unterminated string outright rather than hand back a
 shorter value, so this assertion is belt-and-braces with a compile-time
 check that never runs: either the program fails to build at all, or
 the length matches exactly.)

To 'gen leaf comment lookalike in string' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the remark' is 'gen basics remark'.
    a text called literal is "the ({'the remark'}) reads fine".
    clear 'the basics scratch view'.
    append literal to 'the basics scratch view'.
    a number called 'the expected length' is 'the basics scratch view's size.
    a text called 'the copy name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the length name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the copy declaration' is "{indent}a text called {'the copy name'} is \"{literal}\".\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the copy declaration'.
    a text called 'the buffer declaration' is "{indent}a buffer called {'the length name'} is {'the copy name'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the buffer declaration'.
    a text called 'the size access' is "{'the length name'}'s size".
    a text called 'the assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-14" and 'the size access' and 'the expected length'.
    a text called 'the assertion line' is "{indent}{'the assertion'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the assertion line'.

(BAS-24 (undocumented precision, LANGUAGE.md:81-83): a line of nothing
 but whitespace is a paragraph break; a COMMENT-only line, in the exact
 same position, is not. Placed right after a nested If's own closing
 period - the same trap the blank-line-closes leaves below use - so the
 loop keeps absorbing statements straight through the comment: the lap
 tally must reach the full trip count, proving the comment did not
 eject anything.)

To 'gen leaf comment only line does not close' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_whiles to gen_whiles add 1.
    a number called 'the trips' is 'rng below' of 4 add 2.
    a text called 'the lap name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the inner name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the after name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the remark' is 'gen basics remark'.
    a text called 'the setup' is "{indent}a number called u{gen_whiles} is 0.\n{indent}a number called {'the lap name'} is 0.\n{indent}a number called {'the inner name'} is 0.\n{indent}a number called {'the after name'} is 0.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the setup'.
    a text called body is "{indent}While u{gen_whiles} is less than {'the trips'},\n{indent}  Increment u{gen_whiles},\n{indent}  If u{gen_whiles} is equal to 1 then, Set {'the inner name'} to {'the inner name'} add 1.\n{indent}  ({'the remark'})\n{indent}  Set {'the lap name'} to {'the lap name'} add 1.\n\n".
    'gen emit' of body.
    a text called 'the after action' is "{indent}Set {'the after name'} to {'the after name'} add 1.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the after action'.
    a text called 'the lap assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-24" and 'the lap name' and 'the trips'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the lap assertion'}.\n".
    a text called 'the inner assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-24" and 'the inner name' and 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the inner assertion'}.\n".
    a text called 'the after assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-24" and 'the after name' and 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the after assertion'}.\n".

(BAS-16 (LANGUAGE.md:81): blank lines between two fully-terminated
 TOP-LEVEL statements are optional and change nothing. The manual names
 no upper bound, so the count drawn spans 0 (no blank line at all) up
 to several; the ceiling here is an implementation bound on program
 size, not a reading of the manual, the same way 'gen buffer size's wide
 draw stops at a large number rather than running unbounded.)

To 'gen leaf blank line count invariant' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the tally name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the tally declaration' is "{indent}a number called {'the tally name'} is 0.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the tally declaration'.
    a text called 'the first action' is "{indent}Set {'the tally name'} to {'the tally name'} add 1.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the first action'.
    a number called 'how many blank lines' is 'rng below' of 6.
    a number called 'blank lines placed' is 0.
    While 'blank lines placed' is less than 'how many blank lines',
        'gen emit' of "\n",
        Set 'blank lines placed' to 'blank lines placed' add 1.
    a text called 'the second action' is "{indent}Set {'the tally name'} to {'the tally name'} add 1.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the second action'.
    a text called 'the assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-16" and 'the tally name' and 2.
    a text called 'the assertion line' is "{indent}{'the assertion'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the assertion line'.

(BAS-17 (LANGUAGE.md:83, 150-155): inside an open clause a blank line is
 not cosmetic - it force-closes the clause even when the last body
 action is a nested If already closed by its OWN period (rule 1 only
 pops the If; rule 2's blank line is what pops the loop). The outer
 construct is drawn among the three that iterate; On error gets its own
 leaf below since it does not.)

To 'gen leaf blank line closes nested loop' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the inner name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the after name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the setup' is "{indent}a number called {'the inner name'} is 0.\n{indent}a number called {'the after name'} is 0.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the setup'.
    a number called 'the kind' is 'rng below' of 3.
    If 'the kind' is 0 then,
        'gen leaf blank line closes nested loop while' of indent and 'the inner name'.
    If 'the kind' is 1 then,
        'gen leaf blank line closes nested loop foreach' of indent and 'the inner name'.
    If 'the kind' is 2 then,
        'gen leaf blank line closes nested loop repeat' of indent and 'the inner name'.
    a text called 'the after action' is "{indent}Set {'the after name'} to {'the after name'} add 1.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the after action'.
    a text called 'the inner assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-17" and 'the inner name' and 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the inner assertion'}.\n".
    a text called 'the after assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-17" and 'the after name' and 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the after assertion'}.\n".

To 'gen leaf blank line closes nested loop while' with a text called indent and a text called 'the inner name'.
    Set gen_whiles to gen_whiles add 1.
    a number called 'the trips' is 'rng below' of 4 add 2.
    a text called 'the loop counter declaration' is "{indent}a number called u{gen_whiles} is 0.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the loop counter declaration'.
    a text called body is "{indent}While u{gen_whiles} is less than {'the trips'},\n{indent}  Increment u{gen_whiles},\n{indent}  If u{gen_whiles} is equal to 1 then, Set {'the inner name'} to {'the inner name'} add 1.\n\n".
    'gen emit' of body.

To 'gen leaf blank line closes nested loop foreach' with a text called indent and a text called 'the inner name'.
    a number called 'the trips' is 'rng below' of 4 add 2.
    a text called body is "{indent}For each number from 1 to {'the trips'},\n{indent}  If number is equal to 1 then, Set {'the inner name'} to {'the inner name'} add 1.\n\n".
    'gen emit' of body.

To 'gen leaf blank line closes nested loop repeat' with a text called indent and a text called 'the inner name'.
    Set gen_repeats to gen_repeats add 1.
    a number called 'the trips' is 'rng below' of 4 add 2.
    a text called 'the loop counter declaration' is "{indent}a number called r{gen_repeats} is 0.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the loop counter declaration'.
    a text called body is "{indent}Repeat {'the trips'} times,\n{indent}  Set r{gen_repeats} to r{gen_repeats} add 1,\n{indent}  If r{gen_repeats} is equal to 1 then, Set {'the inner name'} to {'the inner name'} add 1.\n\n".
    'gen emit' of body.

(BAS-41 (LANGUAGE.md:91, 155): the SAME blank line that force-closes an
 open loop also force-closes an enclosing function definition, two
 levels at once. The loop's own state has to live in globals set from
 inside the function and read from outside it - nothing can follow the
 blank line and still count as part of the function's body, which is
 exactly the thing under test: the call and the after-statement below
 only compile at all, at the top level, because the blank line reached
 both clauses together.)

To 'gen leaf blank line closes function too' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_whiles to gen_whiles add 1.
    a text called 'the function name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the inner name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the after name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a number called 'the trips' is 'rng below' of 4 add 2.
    a text called 'the setup' is "{indent}a number called {'the inner name'} is 0.\n{indent}a number called {'the after name'} is 0.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the setup'.
    a text called definition is "{indent}To {'the function name'}.\n{indent}    a number called u{gen_whiles} is 0.\n{indent}    While u{gen_whiles} is less than {'the trips'},\n{indent}        Increment u{gen_whiles},\n{indent}        If u{gen_whiles} is equal to 1 then, Set {'the inner name'} to {'the inner name'} add 1.\n\n".
    'gen emit' of definition.
    a text called call is "{indent}{'the function name'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of call.
    a text called 'the after action' is "{indent}Set {'the after name'} to {'the after name'} add 1.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the after action'.
    a text called 'the inner assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-41" and 'the inner name' and 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the inner assertion'}.\n".
    a text called 'the after assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-41" and 'the after name' and 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the after assertion'}.\n".

(BAS-43 (LANGUAGE.md:169): the blank-line rule applies uniformly across
 while/for each/repeat (the leaf above) and On error too - its body
 force-closes on a blank line the same way, even when its last action is
 a nested If already closed by its own period. The failure is engineered
 (a buffer read past its own size, LANGUAGE.md's own documented
 out-of-range condition) so the handler is guaranteed to fire.)

To 'gen leaf blank line closes on error' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_bufs to gen_bufs add 1.
    a number called 'the buffer size' is 'rng below' of 32 add 4.
    a number called 'the overshoot' is 'rng below' of 100 add 1.
    a number called 'the out-of-range index' is 'the buffer size' add 'the overshoot'.
    a text called 'the caught name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the inner name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the after name' is 'gen flow witness name'.
    a text called 'the setup' is "{indent}a buffer called b{gen_bufs} is {'the buffer size'} bytes in size.\n{indent}a number called {'the caught name'} is 0.\n{indent}a number called {'the inner name'} is 0.\n{indent}a number called {'the after name'} is 0.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the setup'.
    a text called trigger is "{indent}Print byte {'the out-of-range index'} of b{gen_bufs}.\n".
    'gen emit' of trigger.
    a text called body is "{indent}On error\n{indent}  Set {'the caught name'} to {'the caught name'} add 1,\n{indent}  If {'the caught name'} is equal to 1 then, Set {'the inner name'} to {'the inner name'} add 1.\n\n".
    'gen emit' of body.
    a text called 'the after action' is "{indent}Set {'the after name'} to {'the after name'} add 1.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the after action'.
    a text called 'the caught assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-43" and 'the caught name' and 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the caught assertion'}.\n".
    a text called 'the inner assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-43" and 'the inner name' and 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the inner assertion'}.\n".
    a text called 'the after assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "BAS-43" and 'the after name' and 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the after assertion'}.\n".

(BAS-46 (LANGUAGE.md:201-209): the one exception - a blank line placed
 right after a COMMA, with more actions still to come in the same
 sentence, stays purely cosmetic, because the sentence is explicitly
 still open. The lap tally must still reach the full trip count.)

